Does that mean you have osf1 loaded as a module?

The problem above happens when the module isn't loaded.  exec()
doesn't recognize the executable and passes it on to sh, which
chokes of course.

I ran into this when a change to sh broke handling of negations in
pipelines, so loading of the module from rc.alpha would fail.  This
sh bug has been fixed since.

