Two possibilities either you have an ARC console then you can run
update from ARC console, or you have an SRM console then the story
varies a little bit. The following story is about the SRM console.

You shouldn't just copy the file if you have SRM console!

On the Digital's site there is an utility like rawrite (slightly modified)
You can use this utility to write the SRM image to floppy DOS,Win...xxx

You can also use dd on any Unix box to prepare this floppy .
Just take a look in Linux Archives there is information about how to make
the CORRECT boot floppy for booting the SRM console.

And finally on AlphaStation I think you should enable the jumper to allow
boot from floppy and another jumper to allow to flush the chips
(the second one is allowed by factory defaults).

--
Vahe
