You may have to roll-your-own kernel boot command WRT flags and
devices, but AFAIK, the install kernel that RH uses is GENERIC, so it
should work from MILO, assuming the MILO is recent enough.

[NOTE: by "recent enough", I mean that the MILO is known to be able to
 boot a recent kernel that was NOT configured to be built at the "legacy
 start address".]

